{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934611-what-if-the-red-talons-fell-instead-of-the-white-howlers","id":934611,"title":"What if the Red Talons fell instead of the White Howlers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-20T11:17:50-07:00","id":934611,"title":"What if the Red Talons fell instead of the White Howlers?","content":"So, I'm homebrewing a slightly altered WtA setting where the Red Talons fell instead of the Howlers, and I was hoping that someone could help me with ideas for the sorts of differences in this setting- for instance, the Fianna and the Get would not have nearly as much of a rivalry, because the Fianna would have not gone into Harano, and the Get wouldn't have invaded (most likely). Any ideas or thoughts on such a setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:01:27-07:00","id":934633,"title":"","content":"Hm, the entire western Garou race goes extinct because the tribe that is most associated with wild wolf populations turns to the Wyrm? I mean, you might still have the Bunyip, the Croatan, the Hakken, the Uktenu, and the Wendigo, but I would think that the majority of the Old World Garou would have died off because their wolf Kinfolk would have been hunted to extinction by the fallen Red Talons before the discovery' of the New World. In fact, the only Garou left in the Old World by the time of the 'discovery' of the New World would have been the Hakken in Japan because the fallen Red Talons would have likely gone extinct without the new converts that allow the Black Spiral Dancers to thrive.<br /> <br /> Hm, that might have more consequences than you think. Without European Garou slaughtering Australian and Native American Fera and Garou, the indigenous peoples may have been able to resist colonization better. The Camazotz and the Balam may have been able to prevent the colonization of Central and South America (you would not need to have killed that many Europeans during the first century to make people too afraid to come to the continent [a group of four Balam and one Camazotz could have easily slaughtered one hundred men a night and, if you do that once a week, people are going to be afraid]), which would have prevented the annihilation of the Tlacique vampires. The Garou and Fera of North America could have also more effectively organized their Kinfolk against the European invaders. A similar phenomena would have eventually occurred in Australia.<br /> <br /> While nothing would have probably stopped the Europeans from conquering the Caribbean Islands, the lack of European Garou may have stop the colonization of the rest of the Americas and, eventually, the colonization of Australia. The lack of plundered Aztec and Incan gold would have encouraged trade, rather than conquest, with the Native American populations. Spain would have been rapidly replaced in importance as more trade focused European powers at the time (England, Genoa, Netherlands, Portugal, Venice, etc) would have been able to open up the Native American markets to trade in goods. The lack of Native American slaves to fuel the sugar plantations of the Caribbean (which were supplied by genocidal raiding that I am sure that the Native American Garou and Fera would have stopped if not for their attention being distracted by the attacks of the European Garou) would have accelerated the slave trade across the Atlantic by a century. I am not quite sure what the effects would have been after the beginning of the 17th century, as there are too many changes after the first century of contact to predict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:17:00-07:00","id":934642,"title":"","content":"I was toying with the idea of the RT falling later than the WH did, and having the BF take over as the keepers of the Wyld, shifting the Tribal Focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T13:49:42-07:00","id":934694,"title":"","content":"Be careful the idea seems to suggest you just have a personal beef with the murderous purity of the Red Talons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:16:20-07:00","id":934896,"title":"","content":".... And me wanting to homebrew a more interesting Tribe in their place is bad how? I want to give my players the opportunity to play a WH, and most of my players dislike RT. Why make such a rude reply if you don't want to add anything to the post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:38:57-07:00","id":934906,"title":"","content":"While the reply was too strong, I think it was meant to be sarcastic. I have personally never had anyone play a Red Talon in my games. Heck, it is hard enough to get people to play Lupus, regardless of Tribe, because of the Ability restrictions. If you want to have people squirm though, have the beautiful Lupus NPC start sleeping with their Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T21:57:37-07:00","id":934908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheScottishFianna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934611-what-if-the-red-talons-fell-instead-of-the-white-howlers?p=934642#post934642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was toying with the idea of the RT falling later than the WH did, and having the BF take over as the keepers of the Wyld, shifting the Tribal Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>The BFs already had that as their focus since the earliest days of the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T22:04:36-07:00","id":934909,"title":"","content":"I've never really seen that played up, just the protectiveness towards women part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T22:38:16-07:00","id":934918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheScottishFianna</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934611-what-if-the-red-talons-fell-instead-of-the-white-howlers?p=934909#post934909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never really seen that played up, just the protectiveness towards women part.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why they had Wyld Warp and the Red Talons didn't. in Revised, the same was true of Breath of the Wyld, and in W20, Wyld Resurgence. And also why they get the majority of tribal focus in the Book of the Wyld, including awareness of its dangers RE: Thresholds and Abcesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T22:57:22-07:00","id":934925,"title":"","content":"Huh, interesting. Although they would just have more importance in that role I suppose, since the RT would be gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T08:14:44-07:00","id":935077,"title":"","content":"The RT were more the protectors of the wilderness areas and the wild Kinfolk than the protectors of the Wyld, which is why I think the destruction of the RT around the time of the fall of the White Howlers would have resulted in the extinction of the non-Japanese Old World Garou and changed history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T22:01:09-07:00","id":935940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934611-what-if-the-red-talons-fell-instead-of-the-white-howlers?p=935077#post935077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The RT were more the protectors of the wilderness areas and the wild Kinfolk than the protectors of the Wyld, which is why I think the destruction of the RT around the time of the fall of the White Howlers would have resulted in the extinction of the non-Japanese Old World Garou and changed history.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Red Talons traditionally had little to no hold in India, Western or Eastern Asia, or the Middle East really if they can deal with those areas &quot;get across the sea of Japan&quot; isn't going to be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T22:34:11-07:00","id":935946,"title":"","content":"The Hakken survived without lupine kinfolk anyway, so it would not really matter if the RT got to Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T23:03:36-07:00","id":935952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934611-what-if-the-red-talons-fell-instead-of-the-white-howlers?p=935946#post935946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hakken survived without lupine kinfolk anyway, so it would not really matter if the RT got to Japan.</div> </div> </div> </div>No its a problem modern Hakken have because the Japanese Wolf went extinct at the turn of the 20th Century, though w20 had picked up on the Cryptid possibility of them still being alive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T01:29:02-07:00","id":935987,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11866_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11866\" data-vbnamecard=\"11866\">TheScottishFianna</a>, don't sweat the nay-sayers. Some folks approach werewolf with a certain perplexing dogmatism. Have you looked at the 'Tribe Falls' scenario in the (rather confusingly named) Apocalypse source book for WtA? It was made for the Time of Judgement series and it details what could happen when the Talons fall to the Wyrm. Could be some juicy concepts for you to swipe.<br /> <br /> <br /> I am a big fan of the Red Talons, but using them as enemies is better than not using them at all; I don't think it even takes much work- Griffon's children just go from being the friendly opposition to being full antagonists.<br /> <br /> I doubt the Talons would fall to the Wyrm for the same reasons the Howlers did, but there are plenty of openings that might make the Destroyer seem appealing; it could be something as simple as visions of a future without wolves, of a Weaver running rampant and trapping Gaia's face in a mask of steel and asphalt.<br /> <br /> Whatever you choose to do, I look forward to hearing about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T05:44:15-07:00","id":936043,"title":"","content":"And how will they get to Japan when the Moon Bridges are cut? Doggy paddle through Rokea invested waters? I think that the Hakken would be safest group from the RT in the Old World.<br /> <br /> I think that it is an interesting idea that could change history, so you may want to make an alternative WoD. I suggest one where the Garou went mostly extinct in the Old World. The existing Garou would be Australian Aborigine, Japanese, Native American, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T16:47:40-07:00","id":936306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934611-what-if-the-red-talons-fell-instead-of-the-white-howlers?p=936043#post936043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how will they get to Japan when the Moon Bridges are cut? Doggy paddle through Rokea invested waters? I think that the Hakken would be safest group from the RT in the Old World.<br /> <br /> I think that it is an interesting idea that could change history, so you may want to make an alternative WoD. I suggest one where the Garou went mostly extinct in the Old World. The existing Garou would be Australian Aborigine, Japanese, Native American, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are plenty of equally savage terrains in the old world vs a Sea that is readily crossed regularly by people. I'm TOTALLY down with &quot;Europe gets hosed&quot; but There's alot more than Europe. India and SE Asia have sort of the Nagah factor. SE Asia has the Emerald Courts. We could more readily argue a War of Rage that was more costly to the Garou of Europe much like they were practically destroyed in Africa and South America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T10:18:33-07:00","id":936605,"title":"","content":"There'd be no problem. The talons would be rather easy to wipe out, and wouldn't be able to infiltrate human society to the extent of the spiral dancers. Also, if Red Talon dancers would keep to the rule Not being able to recruit homids... <br /> <br /> Every tribe is capable of being your enemy. I actually tend to do the whole 'tribe fighting tribe thing' as part of a central theme of futility to my games. How can you fight the wyrm when you're too busy killing eachother? Garou are stupid, and the real big thing is; If they got along better, they would have won the apocalypse war a long time ago. Between wendigo and talons causing suicidal territory disputes, Glass walkers strengthening the weaver, children of gaia undermining leadership with peace talks (and the Get Laughing at them) and Fera being massive bastards, the problem being your own allies rather than the enemy is a prominent one in all my games. Every tribe is flawed terribly. Capitalize on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T12:34:58-07:00","id":936668,"title":"","content":"How are the Fera massive bastards? The Garou killed them and their kinfolk off, stole their territory, allowed humanity to get out of control, and have not attempted to make amends because, regardless of the situation, they think that they are best shapeshifters for the job. The pride of the Garou prevents them from admitting that they were wrong and, while there are groups of Garou who are willing to apologize (the members of the Beast Courts for example), the western Garou are still unwilling to apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T13:58:09-07:00","id":942226,"title":"","content":"Personally, I could see the European Garou being weaker and relying on humans more, but not totally gone. Just a chunk of the population would go down with maybe the Glass Walkers being the most plentiful. Since the Garou would now be hiding in cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T13:26:45-07:00","id":943817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/934611-what-if-the-red-talons-fell-instead-of-the-white-howlers?p=936668#post936668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are the Fera massive bastards? The Garou killed them and their kinfolk off, stole their territory, allowed humanity to get out of control, and have not attempted to make amends because, regardless of the situation, they think that they are best shapeshifters for the job. The pride of the Garou prevents them from admitting that they were wrong and, while there are groups of Garou who are willing to apologize (the members of the Beast Courts for example), the western Garou are still unwilling to apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fera pride is a real bitch too. Every single Fera thinks it's gaia's No.1 gift. It ain't a problem endemic to just garou. <br /> Also. I'm pretty sure Garou have said sorry. Not all of them, but if a child of gaia hasn't tried then I'll be damned. Fera pride is serious business, I imagine the Bastet probably killed half the Garou who tried to apologise. Fun fact: whilst Fera might be considered a racist word by an sjw, most of the changers have their own 'everything else' word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}